+## Independent reviewer
+
+A fresh, read-only examiner of one bounded change that is isolated from whoever
+produced it: it sees only a sealed package of exact commits, files, and checks,
+and it must not receive the live workspace, prior findings, chat history, or a
+wanted conclusion. A new chat, a prompt that says "be independent," or a claim
+of freshness is not this role; this workflow starts it only when a human
+selects it, and a result that fails isolation is rejected.
+
+**Terminology Source:** This repository (jra-sdd-workflow) — an optional
+isolated review role; "independent" here means isolation from the implementer,
+not "a different conversation."
+
+**Related:** same-session local review, packet (review-ready packet), planning
+review, evidence
+
+## Same-session local review
+
+A review run by an ordinary assistant in the working copy, with normal tools
+and the live files in view — including the packet and any prior findings. It
+can find real problems, but it is not an independent reviewer: even a brand-new
+chat in the same workspace stays this kind of review unless it was launched as
+a sealed, read-only independent review.
+
+**Terminology Source:** This repository (jra-sdd-workflow) — the ordinary
+interactive review worker, contrasted with an independent reviewer.
+
+**Related:** independent reviewer, packet (review-ready packet), planning
+review, taxonomy (defect taxonomy)
 
